    "body": "> If the list holds weak references, it is possible for a MOs that had pending notifications to be GCed before those notifications get processed, which should not be possible.\r\n\r\nThis is not true, because the nodes have [references](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#registered-observer-list) to their corresponding MOs. (Those references get cleared once notifications are delivered.)\r\n\r\nBlink's design is similar to my suggestion in #720, but they make the node -> MO references weak, instead of the global list. That may contribute to the differences discussed in the OP, perhaps.",
